      "content": "\"global white glove\" aesthetic... i like that term. but when you say \"cultural neutrality\" and \"blending in,\" aren't you basically just describing standard Western business attire? like, if someone is in Lagos or Mumbai or even Tokyo, and they wear a tailored blazer and neutral linen trousers to look \"sophisticated,\" aren't they just adopting a Western look? \n\nis there really a way to be \"truly professional\"without just following that Western/European model of dress? or is that just what the global business standard has become?",
